GEO:30.441965;-84.292309
LOCATION:Longmire Recital Hall (LON)
SUMMARY:Discovery Days: "Living Song Project: Healing through the Arts"
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/living-song-project-healing-through-the-arts
CATEGORIES:Arts/Entertainment
CATEGORIES:Music & Concerts
CATEGORIES:Recitals
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261015T234803Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54170372329810
DTSTART:20261021T233000Z
DTEND:20261022T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:This event introduces the Living Song Project (LSP)\, followed by a roughly 45-minute recital shared among four performers and a music therapist\, who will weave improvised guitar and spoken therapeutic narrative between songs\, connecting the music and text to the evening's theme of healing through the arts. The recital is followed by a 20-minute audience-interactive panel discussion\, including a demonstration of the LSP's searchable database and its use in programming the recital\, and a discussion of LSP's potential to support multidisciplinary research and cultural understanding.
GEO:30.441965;-84.292309
LOCATION:Longmire Recital Hall (LON)
SUMMARY:Living Song Project: Healing through the Arts
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/living-song-project-healing-through-the-arts-2392
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261015T234803Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54179886139592
DTSTART:20261023T143000Z
DTEND:20261023T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:This Housewright Virtuoso Series symposium will focus on the limits of knowledge frameworks for music studies in our moment of global transformation. It will feature world-renowned scholars\, including Andrew Chung from the University of North Texas\, Paula Harper from the University of Chicago\, and Gary Tomlinson from Yale University. The panelists will discuss their cutting-edge work on music and the Anthropocene\, digital virality\, and cultural evolution. Together\, we will seek to understand how music is both shaped by and produces dramatic changes in our contemporary world.\n\nAttend in person or virtually!\n\nLivestream: https://www.youtube.com/live/pxNNy4dlmx4
GEO:30.441965;-84.292309
LOCATION:Longmire Recital Hall (LON)
SUMMARY:Musicological Brainfood: Studying Music in the Post-Truth Era
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/musicological-brainfood-studying-music-in-the-post-truth-era
END:VEVENT
